/5/prompt.md:7:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:8:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:9:参考题目如下：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:10:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"1\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"332f06d7\\\" lines=\\\"9-23\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:11:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:12:Slide a solid square through a winding channel to reach a same-sized target square.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:13:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:14:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:15:- bg (most common color). A river color forms a winding corridor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:16:- Two same-sized NxN solid squares on the river: mover and destination, each a distinct color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:17:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:18:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:19:- The mover square travels along the river toward the destination.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:20:- It can only pass through positions where the full NxN area is river.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:21:- If reachable, the mover replaces the destination; otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable point.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:22:- The mover's original position is filled with the river color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:23:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:24:Key insight: Chokepoints narrower than N pixels block the square, forcing it to stop short.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:25:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:26:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:27:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:28:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"2\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"a32d8b75\\\" lines=\\\"262-275\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:29:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:30:Assemble and place enlarged sprites on a canvas using legend-panel instructions.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:31:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:32:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:33:- Color-6 separators divide the grid into a left legend column and a main canvas.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:34:- Each legend panel has (top to bottom): a unit sprite, a frame template, a 5x5 bordered square with a position-marker pixel, and a 3x3 rotation clock-hand.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:35:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:36:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:37:- Tile the unit sprite into each active cell of the frame to build an enlarged composite.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:38:- Rotate the composite per the clock-hand direction (up=0, right=90, down=180, left=270 degrees).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:39:- Place it on the canvas anchored at the position encoded by the marker pixel's row/col in the bordered square's 3x3 inner grid.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:40:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:41:Key insight: The marker pixel's position in a 3x3 grid jointly encodes vertical and horizontal anchor alignment (start/middle/end).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:42:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:43:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:44:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:45:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"3\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"7ed72f31\\\" lines=\\\"8-22\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:46:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:47:Mirror colored sprites using red (2) markers as reflection axes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:48:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:49:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:50:- bg = most common color. Red (2) = marker color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:51:- Colored sprites appear near red markers.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:52:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:53:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:54:- Red line within a sprite (vertical or horizontal) → mirror payload across that axis.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:55:- Single red pixel in a mixed sprite → point-reflect payload around it.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:56:- Isolated red pixel (alone, no payload) → point-reflect each adjacent 8-connected color component.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:57:- Originals remain; mirrored pixels overlay.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:58:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:59:Key insight: Red marker geometry (line vs single pixel) determines reflection type; isolated vs embedded red determines what gets reflected.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:60:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:61:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:62:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:63:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"4\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"6ffbe589\\\" lines=\\\"83-98\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:64:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:65:Crop a board cluster and rotate its color layers based on outside cue sprites.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:66:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:67:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:68:- bg = most common color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:69:- A main multi-color board cluster (largest foreground region).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:70:- Small monochrome cue sprites outside the board for the colors that rotate.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:71:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:72:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:73:- Tight-crop around the board cluster.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:74:- For each color layer inside the crop, find its same-color cue outside.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:75:- Rotate that layer clockwise by (cue pixel count mod 4) × 90°.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:76:- No outside cue → no rotation.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:77:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:78:Key insight: Cue sprite size mod 4 encodes rotation amount for its matching color layer.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:79:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:80:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:81:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:82:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"5\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"a25697e4\\\" lines=\\\"9-23\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:83:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:84:Dock movable tools into border-anchored frames by filling cavities.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:85:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:86:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:87:- bg = most common color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:88:- Border-touching components cluster into anchor frames with interior bg cavities.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:89:- Non-border 2-color components are movable tools.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:90:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:91:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:92:- Match each tool to a frame whose cavity size equals one of its color-region counts.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:93:- Rotate/flip the tool so one color fills the cavity exactly; the other stays outside.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:94:- If the docking orientation uses a reflection, swap the tool's two colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:95:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:96:Key insight: Cavity size determines tool–frame pairing; reflection triggers color swap.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:97:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:98:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:99:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:100:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"6\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"35ab12c3\\\" lines=\\\"73-88\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:101:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:102:Complete outlined shapes and carry attached shadow pixels along their edges.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:103:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:104:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:105:- bg = background. Each active color marks vertices of an 8-direction aligned outline.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:106:- A start vertex can have adjacent non-bg, different-colored shadow pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:107:- Other colored pixels may be distractors unless they lie on valid drawable edges.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:108:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:109:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:110:- For each color, order its pixels by polar angle around their centroid to form a cycle.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:111:- Draw only horizontal, vertical, or 45-degree edges whose interiors are clear.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:112:- From the chosen start vertex, copy adjacent shadow offsets along each drawable edge\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:113:  when the parallel path is in bounds and clear.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:114:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:115:Key insight: The main outline is reconstructed first, then the start vertex's neighbor offsets define parallel shadow strokes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:116:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:117:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:118:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:119:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"7\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"9aaea919\\\" lines=\\\"38-51\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:120:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:121:Transfer sprites from red-marked lanes to green-marked lanes, recoloring and stacking.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:122:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:123:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:124:- bg = most common color. Red (2) and green (3) thin bars define vertical lanes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:125:- Each lane contains repeated identical monochrome sprites in an evenly spaced vertical grid.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:126:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:127:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:128:- Each red lane's sprites turn grey (5); their count transfers to the nearest green lane.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:129:- New sprites fill empty lattice slots bottom-up, using the source shape recolored to the destination lane's sprite color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:130:- All marker bars are removed.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:131:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:132:Key insight: Sprite count is conserved across lanes — red sprites become grey, and equally many new sprites stack into the green lane's regular grid.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:133:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:134:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:135:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:136:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"8\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"88bcf3b4\\\" lines=\\\"229-241\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:137:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:138:Swing an irregular line segment around a nearby obstacle sprite, preserving its pixel count.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:139:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:140:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:141:- bg, bar color (straight lines perpendicular to the grid edge, one end on the border), segment color (irregular stroke attached to bar's inner endpoint), obstacle color (sprite near the bar terminal).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:142:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:143:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:144:- Each bar is perpendicular to the edge it touches; its inner (terminal) endpoint has an attached irregular segment.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:145:- The segment detaches and re-routes: it travels from the terminal toward the nearest obstacle, hugs the obstacle's boundary, then exits at a 45° diagonal.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:146:- Total painted pixels equal the original segment length.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:147:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:148:Key insight: The segment behaves like a rope swung around the obstacle — attach at the nearest point, trace the skin, exit diagonally, conserving length.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:149:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:150:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:151:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:152:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"9\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"8b9c3697\\\" lines=\\\"9-23\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:153:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:154:Insert red components into interior sockets of large structures, leaving a black trail.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:155:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:156:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:157:- bg = most common. Large non-bg, non-red structures with interior cavities.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:158:- Red components outside structures.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:159:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:160:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:161:- Interior sockets: bg cells inside a structure's bbox, adjacent to structure pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:162:- For each structure, find the direction where rays from sockets hit a red component.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:163:- Slide that component into the socket; paint traversed cells black.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:164:- Unmatched reds vanish.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:165:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:166:Key insight: Docking direction is inferred by ray-casting from interior sockets to the nearest red component.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:167:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:168:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:169:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:170:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"10\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"b0039139\\\" lines=\\\"29-44\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:171:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:172:Recolor a cropped template and repeat it according to a component-count stencil.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:173:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:174:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:175:- Solid blue (1) separator rows or columns split the grid into four sections.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:176:- Section 1 is a black-background shape template; section 2 is a component-count stencil.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:177:- Sections 3 and 4 are solid color swatches for output foreground and background.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:178:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:179:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:180:- Crop section 1 to the bbox of its non-black pixels and recolor it with the two swatches.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:181:- Count 4-connected non-black components in section 2.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:182:- Repeat the recolored crop that many times, inserting one background-colored row/column between copies.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:183:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:184:Key insight: The second section encodes only the repeat count; the output orientation\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:185:is inherited from whether the input separators are columns or rows.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:186:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:187:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:188:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:189:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"11\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"247ef758\\\" lines=\\\"35-46\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:190:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:191:Move colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:192:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:193:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:194:- bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:195:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:196:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:197:- For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:198:- Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:199:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:200:Key insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:201:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:202:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:203:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:204:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"12\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"7b5033c1\\\" lines=\\\"7-21\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:205:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:206:Straighten a colored snake path into a single-column strip preserving pixel order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:207:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:208:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:209:- bg = most common color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:210:- Non-bg pixels form a single 4-connected path (snake) with exactly two endpoints.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:211:- Each path pixel may be a different non-bg color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:212:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:213:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:214:- Find the two endpoints (cells with only one path neighbor) of the snake.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:215:- Begin at the top-left-most endpoint and trace the path cell by cell.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:216:- Output an (N×1) column listing each cell's color in traversal order.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:217:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:218:Key insight: The path is a simple chain with no branches; choosing the top-left-most endpoint fixes a unique reading direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:219:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:220:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:221:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:222:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"13\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"f931b4a8\\\" lines=\\\"10-27\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:223:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:224:Count the two upper quadrant control regions to size an output made from the lower quadrant pattern.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:225:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:226:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:227:- The grid is an even square split into four equal quadrants.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:228:- Black is the background.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:229:- The upper-left and upper-right quadrants are control regions.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:230:- The lower-left quadrant is a color source tile; the lower-right quadrant is either a stencil tile or empty.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:231:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:232:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:233:- Output height is the number of non-background pixels in the upper-left quadrant.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:234:- Output width is the number of non-background pixels in the upper-right quadrant.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:235:- If the lower-right stencil has foreground pixels, tile it over the output; each stencil background pixel is filled from the lower-left quadrant cell at the corresponding coarse tile position.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:236:- If the lower-right stencil is empty, tile the lower-left quadrant directly over the output.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:237:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:238:Key insight:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:239:- The top quadrants specify only dimensions, while the bottom quadrants specify a two-level repeated pattern: a fine stencil and coarse fill colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:240:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:241:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:242:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:243:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"14\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"16de56c4\\\" lines=\\\"9-34\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:244:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:245:Fill periodic progressions that shoot from a unique grid edge.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:246:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:247:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:248:- bg = most common color.  Sparse non-bg dots of several colors.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:249:- All repeating colors originate from the same grid edge (top, bottom,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:250:  left, or right — the one with the most non-bg dots).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:251:- Each repeating color has exactly 2 dots per shooting-direction line;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:252:  their gap defines the step.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:253:- Every non-bg dot lies on a shooting-direction line that contains a\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:254:  repeating color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:255:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:256:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:257:- Determine the unique shooting edge; left/right → rows, top/bottom → columns.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:258:- For each shooting-direction line, the repeating color has exactly 2 dots;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:259:  step = gap between them, offset = first position mod step.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:260:- A different-colored dot aligned to the same beat (pos % step == offset) is\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:261:  a companion: it absorbs the ray and becomes the fill color, limiting the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:262:  fill range to the span between repeating and companion dots.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:263:- An unaligned dot is a bystander and left untouched.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:264:- Without a companion the repeating color fills the entire line.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:265:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:266:Key insight: the shooting edge is identified by counting boundary dots;\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:267:the gap between the two marker dots is the period; a companion sharing the\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:268:modular class acts as a wall that stops the ray and dictates the paint color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:269:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:270:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:271:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:272:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"15\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"c7f57c3e\\\" lines=\\\"22-35\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:273:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:274:Swap every sprite to the opposite prototype while preserving scale and position.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:275:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:276:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:277:- bg = most common color. Two distinct small sprite patterns (prototypes) appear at various scales.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:278:- Each sprite instance is a scaled copy of one of the two prototypes, placed on the grid.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:279:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:280:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:281:- Identify the two prototype patterns from the smallest-area sprites.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:282:- For each sprite, determine which prototype it matches and its integer scale factor.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:283:- Replace it with the other prototype at the same scale, aligned by an internal anchor region (color-1 pixels).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:284:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:285:Key insight: Every sprite toggles to the alternate prototype; the anchor sub-region inside each sprite pins the alignment so swapped sprites land in the correct position regardless of scale.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:286:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:287:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:288:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:289:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"16\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"e3721c99\\\" lines=\\\"69-83\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:290:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:291:Recolor grey shapes by matching their hole count to a color legend.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:292:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:293:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:294:- bg = most common color; grey (5) sprites scattered across the grid.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:295:- Colored legend shapes (non-bg, non-grey, at least 2×2, not touching the outer border) near grid edge,\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:296:  each with a distinct number of enclosed holes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:297:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:298:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:299:- Each colored legend shape defines a mapping: hole count → color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:300:- For every grey sprite, count its holes (enclosed bg regions not touching the sprite's bounding-box border).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:301:- Recolor the grey sprite to the matching legend color; erase grey distractors with unlisted hole counts.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:302:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:303:Key insight: Shape identity is encoded by topology (number of holes), not geometry or size.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:304:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:305:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:306:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:307:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"17\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"edb79dae\\\" lines=\\\"39-53\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:308:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:309:Stamp recolored sprites into a framed region using placeholder positions and a color legend.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:310:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:311:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:312:- bg background, a rectangular single-color frame, colored placeholder cells inside the frame.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:313:- Outside the frame: sprite shapes (one per placeholder color) and a small legend mapping each placeholder color to an output color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:314:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:315:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:316:- Find the frame and its interior placeholders.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:317:- For each placeholder color, locate the matching-color sprite outside the frame.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:318:- Stamp each sprite at the placeholder's position inside the frame.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:319:- Recolor every stamped sprite to the output color defined by the legend.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:320:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:321:Key insight: The legend pairs (overlapping two-color glyphs outside the frame) dictate the final recoloring — placeholder color selects the shape, legend maps it to the output color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:322:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:323:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:324:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:325:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"18\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"409aa875\\\" lines=\\\"68-81\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:326:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:327:Fire projectiles from 3-pixel triangle sprites; mark collisions with maroon or blue.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:328:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:329:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:330:- bg = most common color. Non-bg 3-pixel sprites shaped as axis-aligned L's or diagonal V's.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:331:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:332:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:333:- Each triangle has an apex and an emission direction determined by its shape: L-shapes fire diagonally away from the missing corner; V-shapes fire along the axis away from the open side.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:334:- A projectile lands exactly 5 cells from the apex in the emission direction.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:335:- If it hits an existing sprite, that entire sprite is recolored to maroon (9).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:336:- If two projectiles land on the same empty cell, that cell becomes blue (1); a lone projectile on empty bg paints maroon (9).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:337:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:338:Key insight: The triangle's orientation encodes both direction and target; dual-projectile collisions on open bg produce blue, not maroon.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:339:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:340:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:341:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:342:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"19\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"13e47133\\\" lines=\\\"56-69\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:343:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:344:Fill partitioned regions with concentric colored bands derived from marker pixels.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:345:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:346:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:347:- Grid partitioned into regions by wall-colored lines.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:348:- Each region has a dominant base color and a few isolated marker pixels of other colors at varying depths from the region boundary.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:349:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:350:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:351:- For each region, read marker colors ordered by their Chebyshev distance from the boundary to build a color palette.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:352:- If no marker sits on the boundary itself, the base color leads the palette.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:353:- Paint every cell with palette[distance mod palette_length], producing repeating concentric rectangular frames that radiate inward.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:354:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:355:Key insight: Each marker's depth from the boundary defines its position in the cyclic palette; the pattern then tiles inward automatically.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:356:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:357:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:358:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:359:<reference_puzzle index=\\\"20\\\" source=\\\"eval\\\" puzzle_id=\\\"2d0172a1\\\" lines=\\\"209-224\\\">\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:360:<description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:361:Convert a rough nested line drawing into a clean canonical frame-and-dot diagram.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:362:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:363:Input structure:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:364:- The grid has one background color and one foreground color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:365:- Foreground 4-connected objects are rough closed frames or small filled blobs.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:366:- Frames may contain other frames/blobs; blobs outside a frame remain outside it.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:367:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:368:Rule:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:369:- Detect the containment tree of foreground objects using holes of each frame object.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:370:- Replace every blob with one foreground pixel.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:371:- Replace every frame with a rectangular border padded two cells around its direct children.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:372:- Place siblings by their original row/column overlap and order, with one empty cell between canonical objects.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:373:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:374:Key insight: The exact wobbly geometry is irrelevant; only enclosure plus relative sibling positions define the output.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:375:</description>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:376:</reference_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:377:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:378:你的任务：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:379:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:380:创新方式包括但不限于：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:381:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:382:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:383:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考\\\"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程\\\"。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:384:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:385:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:386:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:387:<new_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:388:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:389:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:390:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:391:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:392:</new_puzzle>\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:393:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:394:请一次性生成 5 个 `<new_puzzle>`，若有较多合适的创新，也可以生成更多，不设上限，但不要输出额外解释。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:395:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:396:注意事项：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:397:1. 任务不应依赖大量先验知识或复杂计算，而应依赖对模式、结构与空间关系的直觉推理。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:398:2. 关于\\\"计算\\\"的边界：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:399:   - **允许使用**（这些都是人类能心算的视觉量）：数像素 / 孔洞 / 对象 / 邻居（≤10 量级）、比大小、按某个可见属性排序、奇偶判断、取最大 / 最小、用一个计数值作为另一个等量几何量（如 N 个像素 → 长度 N 的射线、面积 N → 边长 N）、判断接触 / 相邻 / 包含、粗略中心位置（簇的视觉中点）、\\\"距离\\\"作为\\\"几步\\\"而不是公式等人类能够直观感受计算的内容。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:400:   - **禁止使用**（这些是算法量而非视觉量，会迫使解题者依赖公式而非视觉直觉）：曼哈顿 / 欧氏 / Chebyshev 距离作为精确查表键、凸包面积、二进制位编码 / 位运算、模运算（取模） / 余数、拓扑距离（BFS / 最短路 / 跳数）、精确几何质心坐标、凸角 / 凹角计数等复杂且不易被看出来的计算都是禁止使用的。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:401:3. 问题必须能从少量示例中推断出来（通常为 3 对训练样例 + 1 个测试样例）。设计时从人类解题者的视觉角度思考：规则涉及的所有关键要素（对象、关系、属性）必须在网格上肉眼可见，不应依赖人眼无法直接观察到的隐含信息（例如颜色id和颜色亮度是禁止使用的）或需要推算的隐藏属性。规则背后的逻辑本身可以有一定挑战性，但解题所需的所有线索必须能从网格中直接获取。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:402:4. 生成的问题描述旨在促进后续用于创建题目网格的代码生成。因此，对输入 / 输出网格的描述以及规则总结必须极其详细；语言风格应易于理解；对于特定对象（如箭头），必须在描述中明确其绘制方式。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:403:5. 描述谜题时避免使用 0 或 1 这类颜色编号；应使用颜色名称，例如 \\\"red\\\"。可用颜色如下：Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:404:6. 5 个新题的核心推理机制应明显不同——即从观察样例到归纳规则的认知路径不同，而不仅仅是场景、对象或颜色不同。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:405:7. 题目难度应来自机制的隐蔽性而非步骤数。用参考题作为难度标尺——如果你生成的题一个样例就能猜到规则，说明机制太透明，需要加深隐蔽性。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:406:8. 优先从参考题的机制出发进行重组或推演，而非从物理隐喻出发。物理隐喻容易导致大量题目归结为一种模式，例如\\\"沿方向移动到阻挡处停止\\\"。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:407:9. 题目的难度优先来自规则的**结构层数**，而不是单一步骤的复杂度。关于\\\"结构层数\\\"的判定标准：**只有解题者需要主动推理才能完成的步骤才算一层**。肉眼一扫即可获得的信息（如\\\"找到缺口在哪一侧\\\"、\\\"数出像素个数\\\"、\\\"识别哪个对象最大\\\"）不构成独立的推理层——它们只是变换的前置输入，不增加认知难度。真正的多层结构是指每一层都需要解题者发现一个非显然的规律。以两层结构为例：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:408:   - ✗ 伪两层：\\\"找到缺口方向\\\"→\\\"把东西推到对面\\\" — 第一步肉眼可见，实际只有一层推理。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:409:   - ✓ 真两层：\\\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\\\"→\\\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\\\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:410:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:411:   如果你发现自己写出的题只是\\\"对每个对象，根据它的某个属性做某变换\\\"的单步规则，请引入一个需要主动推理的前置步骤。**用堆叠 tie-break 规则或复杂数学公式来\\\"加难度\\\"是劣解；用多一层需要归纳的结构嵌套来\\\"加难度\\\"才是好解**。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:412:10. 在符合ARC题目和提示词要求的基础上，鼓励尝试创新规则为多层结构的题目，不局限于两层，可以创新三层或四层结构的题目，但不可为了多结构层数违背要求。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:413:\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:414:生成后对生成的题执行以下四项审查（审查内容不需要保存到文件）：\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:415:1. 原创性\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:416:  新题不可与上述参考题相同或类似，不可只是替换颜色、方向、对象类型等表层要素。判断标准：新题的核心推理路径应与任何一道参考题不同。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:417:2. 确定性\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:418:  规则完全确定，同一输入只能产生唯一输出，每一步操作都有明确定义。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:419:3. 可实现性\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:420:  所有必要细节都已给出——对象如何生成、如何识别、如何变换、边界情况如何处理，读完描述后可以直接写代码。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:421:4. ARC 合规性\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed720058768/5/prompt.md:422:  网格尺寸合理（≤30×30），使用颜色不超过 10 种，规则复杂度适中，人类能从 3-5 个样例中发现规律。没有使用上述注意事项第二条禁止使用