t common color.\\n  47:     - Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\\n  48:     - Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\\n  49: \\n  50:     Rule:\\n  51:     - Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\\n  52:     - Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\\n  53:     - Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\\n  54: \\n  55:     Key insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\\n  56:     \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n  57:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\n  58:     h, w = g.shape\\n  59:     bg = get_bg(g)\\n  60: \\n  61:     out = g.copy()\\n  62: \\n  63:     # Precompute background regions (4-connected). Exclude those containing background corners as \\\"outside\\\".\\n  64:     bg_comps = _components_mask(g == bg, conn8=False)\\n  65:     regions = []  # list of (set_pts, boundary_set, touches_border, size)\\n  66:     for pts in bg_comps:\\n  67:         region = set(pts)\\n  68:         touches = _touches_border(pts, h, w)\\n  69:         boundary = set()\\n  70:         for r, c in region:\\n  71:             for nr, nc in neighbors4(r, c):\\n  72:                 if 0 <= nr < h and 0 <= nc < w and (nr, nc) not in region and int(g[nr, nc]) != bg:\\n  73:                     boundary.add((nr, nc))\\n  74:         regions.append((region, boundary, touches, len(region)))\\n  75: \\n  76:     corners = {(0, 0), (0, w - 1), (h - 1, 0), (h - 1, w - 1)}\\n  77:     outside_idxs = set()\\n  78:     for i, (reg, _, _, _) in enumerate(regions):\\n  79:         if any(p in reg for p in corners if int(g[p]) == bg):\\n  80:             outside_idxs.add(i)\\n  81: \\n  82:     cavities = []\\n  83:     for i, (reg, bnd, _, _) in enumerate(regions):\\n  84:         if i in outside_idxs or not bnd:\\n  85:             continue\\n  86:         bcols = {int(g[p]) for p in bnd}\\n  87:         cavities.appe